body:
New reading from a user (relayed 2026-11-16): **closing and opening the project again clears the slowness.**

This points to state that grows during a session, not to the cost of the project itself. A freshly opened project with the same operations is fast. Check for:
- toolpath, overlay or label meshes that are created again on each edit, generate or selection, while the old ones are not freed (a leak: AGENTS.md says a leak is a critical bug);
- caches or per-operation GPU buffers keyed by something that changes on each regenerate, so they grow without limit;
- callbacks, observers or systems registered again on each operation add, so each frame runs them several times.

A useful pin: add and regenerate operations in a loop in a test session, then compare the count of live meshes, GPU buffers, or per-frame system runs with a session that opens the same project fresh.
